From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dallas Delaney <dadelan@microsoft.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 06:51:23 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] erofs: discover and validate signed dm-verity referrers

Discover dm-verity referrers for image layers, validate and retain the
signed root-hash metadata, and derive per-layer snapshot identities so
unpacked layers are bound to the signatures they were verified against.

Wire the CRI path end to end: the transfer service pull discovers
referrers when the unpack snapshotter advertises the dm-verity referrer
capability and records the selected bundle on the image record. Unpack
trusts a signed target only when discovery validated it, and container
creation resolves the signed snapshot key so CRI consumes the signed
chain.

Qualify the unpack snapshot GC edge by manifest digest rather than chain
ID so re-signing the same manifest replaces the edge instead of leaking
the superseded snapshot, while distinct manifests sharing a config keep
independent edges.

Registry-supplied target annotations are stripped before unpack, so a
layer without a validated target takes the ordinary path. Unsigned EROFS
and OverlayFS behavior is unchanged.

Co-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>
